      "message": "fix(slice): section touching or stacked solids as their union\n\nA soup that meets a slice plane 3+ ways is retried as the union of its\nclosed solids: facets are split into bodies by shared-edge connectivity\n(corners welded within 0.1 um), and only when every body is a closed,\nconsistently wound 2-manifold with positive volume is each body sliced\nalone and the sections united. Anything else - solids welded along a\nshared edge or face, an open body, an inward cavity shell - keeps the\nnon-manifold refusal, now worded as the model's fault with the fix.\nMeshes that sliced before never reach the fallback.\n\nThe generators map Open/NonManifold slice faults to a new\nGenError::Model (\"the source model cannot be sliced: ...\") instead of\n\"invalid machining parameters\".\n\nThe touching-bodies section readers (material_above_of,\nmaterial_overhead_of) move to slice_bodies with the fallback, re-exported\nfrom slice (400-line law).\n\nFixes #1407\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
